      "result": "Contents of https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/javascript/api/@azure/arm-storage/storageaccountcreateparameters?view=azure-node-latest:\nThe parameters used when creating a storage account.\n\n## Properties\n\n[accessTier](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-accesstier)\n\nRequired for storage accounts where kind = BlobStorage. The access tier is used for billing. The 'Premium' access tier is the default value for premium block blobs storage account type and it cannot be changed for the premium block blobs storage account type.\n\n[allowBlobPublicAccess](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-allowblobpublicaccess)\n\nAllow or disallow public access to all blobs or containers in the storage account. The default interpretation is false for this property.\n\n[allowCrossTenantReplication](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-allowcrosstenantreplication)\n\nAllow or disallow cross AAD tenant object replication. Set this property to true for new or existing accounts only if object replication policies will involve storage accounts in different AAD tenants. The default interpretation is false for new accounts to follow best security practices by default.\n\n[allowedCopyScope](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-allowedcopyscope)\n\nRestrict copy to and from Storage Accounts within an AAD tenant or with Private Links to the same VNet.\n\n[allowSharedKeyAccess](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-allowsharedkeyaccess)\n\nIndicates whether the storage account permits requests to be authorized with the account access key via Shared Key. If false, then all requests, including shared access signatures, must be authorized with Azure Active Directory (Azure AD). The default value is null, which is equivalent to true.\n\n[azureFilesIdentityBasedAuthentication](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-azurefilesidentitybasedauthentication)\n\nProvides the identity based authentication settings for Azure Files.\n\n[customDomain](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-customdomain)\n\nUser domain assigned to the storage account. Name is the CNAME source. Only one custom domain is supported per storage account at this time. To clear the existing custom domain, use an empty string for the custom domain name property.\n\n[defaultToOAuthAuthentication](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-defaulttooauthauthentication)\n\nA boolean flag which indicates whether the default authentication is OAuth or not. The default interpretation is false for this property.\n\n[dnsEndpointType](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-dnsendpointtype)\n\nAllows you to specify the type of endpoint. Set this to AzureDNSZone to create a large number of accounts in a single subscription, which creates accounts in an Azure DNS Zone and the endpoint URL will have an alphanumeric DNS Zone identifier.\n\n[dualStackEndpointPreference](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-dualstackendpointpreference)\n\nMaintains information about the Internet protocol opted by the user.\n\n[enableExtendedGroups](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-enableextendedgroups)\n\nEnables extended group support with local users feature, if set to true\n\n[enableHttpsTrafficOnly](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-enablehttpstrafficonly)\n\nAllows https traffic only to storage service if sets to true. The default value is true since API version 2019-04-01.\n\n[enableNfsV3](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-enablenfsv3)\n\nNFS 3.0 protocol support enabled if set to true.\n\n[encryption](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-encryption)\n\nEncryption settings to be used for server-side encryption for the storage account.\n\n[extendedLocation](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-extendedlocation)\n\nOptional. Set the extended location of the resource. If not set, the storage account will be created in Azure main region. Otherwise it will be created in the specified extended location\n\n[geoPriorityReplicationStatus](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-geopriorityreplicationstatus)\n\nStatus indicating whether Geo Priority Replication is enabled for the account.\n\n[identity](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-identity)\n\nThe identity of the resource.\n\n[immutableStorageWithVersioning](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-immutablestoragewithversioning)\n\nThe property is immutable and can only be set to true at the account creation time. When set to true, it enables object level immutability for all the new containers in the account by default.\n\n[isHnsEnabled](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-ishnsenabled)\n\nAccount HierarchicalNamespace enabled if sets to true.\n\n[isLocalUserEnabled](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-islocaluserenabled)\n\nEnables local users feature, if set to true\n\n[isSftpEnabled](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-issftpenabled)\n\nEnables Secure File Transfer Protocol, if set to true\n\n[keyPolicy](#@azure-arm-storage-storageaccountcreateparameters-keypolicy)\n\nKeyPolicy assigned\n\n\u003cnote\u003eContent truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 5000 to get more content.\u003c/note\u003e"
